ds. We then show that there are no solutions with $\\alpha>0$ on certain ample line bundles over certain toric manifolds and compute the value of $\\alpha$ if a solution exists. We also relate our result to the existence result of Keller-Friedman in dimension-two.","id":"af52ed31-75ba-4532-af20-475bc645f400","capacityId":"af52ed31-75ba-4532-af20-475bc645f400","name":"A Formula for the $\\alpha$-Futaki Character","status":2,"type":"Session","defaultFeeId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","fees":{},"closedReasonType":"NotClosed","isOpenForRegistration":false,"presentationType":"","categoryId":"dd348cad-9fa9-4bfb-8f6b-0d76eda0f5fe","capacity":269,"waitlistCapacityId":"af52ed31-75ba-4532-af20-475bc645f400_waitlist","dataTagCode":"","startTime":"2026-07-26T17:10:00.000Z","endTime":"2026-07-26T17:30:00.000Z","locationId":"002ab162-a334-43ba-82fb-22118ca06cc8","locationName":"115-C","locationCode":"115-C","isIncludedSession":false,"isWaitlistEnabled":false,"registeredCount":4,"associatedWithAdmissionItems":[],"availableToAdmissionItems":[],"associatedRegistrationTypes":[],"sessionCustomFieldValues":{"1ff8930b-09e9-45ce-993d-1226c743588b":{"id":"1ff8930b-09e9-45ce-993d-1226c743588b","sessionId":"af52ed31-75ba-4532-af20-475bc645f400","displayValue":"Kartick Ghosh","answers":["Kartick Ghosh"]},"ed161947-576f-4a6a-a4e1-5d22ce5a1203":{"id":"ed161947-576f-4a6a-a4e1-5d22ce5a1203","sessionId":"af52ed31-75ba-4532-af20-475bc645f400","displayValue":"5 - Geometry","answers":["5 - Geometry"]}},"registrantInformation":"","displayPriority":0,"showOnAgenda":true,"isOpenForAttendeeHub":true,"featuredSession":false,"speakerIds":{"fd8d3428-29b9-4a80-8d87-6ce3e2d0a929":{"speakerId":"fd8d3428-29b9-4a80-8d87-6ce3e2d0a929","speakerCategoryId":"ab3cd2dc-d1f9-4200-a5a7-26b170cec2fb","sessionId":"af52ed31-75ba-4532-af20-475bc645f400","sessionSpeakerOrder":0}},"documents":{},"createdDate":"2026-05-16T11:34:17.600Z","restrictSessionVisibility":true},"ae721be8-2830-46ae-8a0a-788acfc1a690":{"code":"AfonsoBandeiraSession","description":"<div class=\"ag87-crtemvc-hsbk\">Random matrix theory has played a major role in several areas of pure and applied mathematics, as well as statistics, physics, and computer science. This lecture aims to describe the intrinsic freeness phenomenon and how it provides new easy-to-use sharp non-asymptotic bounds on the spectrum of general random matrices.We will also present a couple of illustrative applications in high dimensional statistical inference.</div>","id":"ae721be8-2830-46ae-8a0a-788acfc1a690","capacityId":"ae721be8-2830-46ae-8a0a-788acfc1a690","name":"Random Matrices, Intrinsic Freeness, and Sharp Non-Asymptotic Inequalities","status":2,"type":"Session","defaultFeeId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","fees":{},"closedReasonType":"NotClosed","isOpenForRegistration":false,"presentationType":"","categoryId":"7ac6a87e-8daa-4742-9215-4437219ac29a","waitlistCapacityId":"ae721be8-2830-46ae-8a0a-788acfc1a690_waitlist","dataTagCode":"","startTime":"2026-07-24T21:00:00.000Z","endTime":"2026-07-24T21:45:00.000Z","locationId":"832094e7-0e57-4e55-8e2e-d69b459e2551","locationName":"116-A","locationCode":"116-A","isIncludedSession":false,"isWaitlistEnabled":false,"registeredCount":28,"associatedWithAdmissionItems":[],"availableToAdmissionItems":[],"associatedRegistrationTypes":[],"sessionCustomFieldValues":{"1ff8930b-09e9-45ce-993d-1226c743588b":{"id":"1ff8930b-09e9-45ce-993d-1226c743588b","sessionId":"ae721be8-2830-46ae-8a0a-788acfc1a690","displayValue":"Afonso Bandeira","answers":["Afonso Bandeira"]},"ed161947-576f-4a6a-a4e1-5d22ce5a1203":{"id":"ed161947-576f-4a6a-a4e1-5d22ce5a1203","sessionId":"ae721be8-2830-46ae-8a0a-788acfc1a690","displayValue":"17 - Statistics| Machine Learning | Image | Signal Processing","answers":["17 - Statistics| Machine Learning | Image | Signal Processing"]}},"richTextDescription":"Random matrix theory has played a major role in several areas of pure and applied mathematics, as well as statistics, physics, and computer science. This lecture aims to describe the intrinsic freeness phenomenon and how it provides new easy-to-use sharp non-asymptotic bounds on the spectrum of general random matrices.We will also present a couple of illustrative applications in high dimensional statistical inference.","plainTextDescription":"Random matrix theory has played a major role in several areas of pure and applied mathematics, as well as statistics, physics, and computer science. This lecture aims to describe the intrinsic freeness phenomenon and how it provides new easy-to-use sharp non-asymptotic bounds on the spectrum of general random matrices.We will also present a couple of illustrative applications in high dimensional statistical inference.","registrantInformation":"","displayPriority":0,"showOnAgenda":true,"isOpenForAttendeeHub":true,"featuredSession":false,"speakerIds":{"849ee3f2-8e80-4ee1-99dd-62b0f68ea4a2":{"speakerId":"849ee3f2-8e80-4ee1-99dd-62b0f68ea4a2","speakerCategoryId":"45ab9016-e39c-4327-8bdb-50c0e5f04916","sessionId":"ae721be8-2830-46ae-8a0a-788acfc1a690","sessionSpeakerOrder":1}},"documents":{},"createdDate":"2025-04-11T14:49:56.810Z","restrictSessionVisibility":true},"a8cd13d4-19c0-4a6b-af48-8cbf1edea54d":{"code":"SCEKARAPINARSESSION","description":"<div class=\"ag87-crtemvc-hsbk\">This talk aims to reveal the dilemmas of the fixed point theorems that were first constructed by Banach in 1922. It is possible to transform many of the real-world problems into fixed-point theorems. This shows how the fixed point theory is useful and how huge the application potential is. On the other hand, a lot of results are repeated in this theory, which is of great interest. A substantial part of the new results suggested overlaps with the old results.To support this observation,   a few examples from the current literature will be shared.</div>","id":"a8cd13d4-19c0-4a6b-af48-8cbf1edea54d","capacityId":"a8cd13d4-19c0-4a6b-af48-8cbf1edea54d","name":"XXX Remarks on Re