ned over bicentric quadrilaterals inscribed in the unit disk, containing the origin. We then provide a sharp estimate for the Gaussian curvature of these minimal surfaces at the point above the origin. Our proof employs complex-analytic methods, as the minimal surfaces in question allow a conformal harmonic parameterization.","id":"f2ad0e5d-196e-4d60-be44-16af347cc49a","capacityId":"f2ad0e5d-196e-4d60-be44-16af347cc49a","name":"Hopf Conjecture for Gaussian Curvature of Minimal Graphs","status":2,"type":"Session","defaultFeeId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","fees":{},"closedReasonType":"NotClosed","isOpenForRegistration":false,"presentationType":"","categoryId":"dd348cad-9fa9-4bfb-8f6b-0d76eda0f5fe","capacity":629,"waitlistCapacityId":"f2ad0e5d-196e-4d60-be44-16af347cc49a_waitlist","dataTagCode":"","startTime":"2026-07-28T15:30:00.000Z","endTime":"2026-07-28T15:50:00.000Z","locationId":"18f6e81f-a563-4e79-a907-872c0f1b59a7","locationName":"119-AB","locationCode":"119-AB","isIncludedSession":false,"isWaitlistEnabled":false,"registeredCount":5,"associatedWithAdmissionItems":[],"availableToAdmissionItems":[],"associatedRegistrationTypes":[],"sessionCustomFieldValues":{"1ff8930b-09e9-45ce-993d-1226c743588b":{"id":"1ff8930b-09e9-45ce-993d-1226c743588b","sessionId":"f2ad0e5d-196e-4d60-be44-16af347cc49a","displayValue":"David Kalaj","answers":["David Kalaj"]},"ed161947-576f-4a6a-a4e1-5d22ce5a1203":{"id":"ed161947-576f-4a6a-a4e1-5d22ce5a1203","sessionId":"f2ad0e5d-196e-4d60-be44-16af347cc49a","displayValue":"8 - Analysis","answers":["8 - Analysis"]}},"registrantInformation":"","displayPriority":0,"showOnAgenda":true,"isOpenForAttendeeHub":true,"featuredSession":false,"speakerIds":{"365639ec-cacf-4a4d-af3c-5ef3259c73a3":{"speakerId":"365639ec-cacf-4a4d-af3c-5ef3259c73a3","speakerCategoryId":"ab3cd2dc-d1f9-4200-a5a7-26b170cec2fb","sessionId":"f2ad0e5d-196e-4d60-be44-16af347cc49a","sessionSpeakerOrder":0}},"documents":{},"createdDate":"2026-05-16T11:46:06.753Z","restrictSessionVisibility":true},"6fc13d53-6c76-4415-8dd6-32d6ba57f750":{"code":"MATHFEST1","description":"<div class=\"ag87-crtemvc-hsbk\"><div class=\"css-vsf5of\"><p class=\"carina-rte-public-DraftStyleDefault-block\">Join us in Hall E for a family-friendly Math Festival open to the public. This interactive celebration of mathematics will feature hands-on activities, engaging talks, games and art designed to inspire curiosity and showcase the beauty and creativity of math for all ages. Discover how mathematics connects to everyday life, science, and culture while experiencing the excitement of one of the world’s largest gatherings of mathematicians.</p><p class=\"carina-rte-public-DraftStyleDefault-block\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">MathHappens Activity Area</span></p><ul class=\"carina-rte-public-DraftStyleDefault-ul\"><li>Multi-station interactive math playground featuring puzzles, tiles, and tactile models that encourage exploration, pattern recognition, and informal learning through hands-on discovery.</li></ul><p class=\"carina-rte-public-DraftStyleDefault-block\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Maze Mat / Twist-n-Roll / Ring of Fire</span></p><ul class=\"carina-rte-public-DraftStyleDefault-ul\"><li>Dynamic large-scale interactive math installations including floor-based mazes, tactile exhibits, and collaborative builds designed for full-body engagement and high visitor throughput.</li></ul><p class=\"carina-rte-public-DraftStyleDefault-block\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Probability Power / Clothesline of Chance</span></p><ul class=\"carina-rte-public-DraftStyleDefault-ul\"><li>Interactive game-show style probability experience where participants engage in live challenges (coin flipping + probability ranking) to build intuition around chance and real-world likelihood (close line).</li></ul><p class=\"carina-rte-public-DraftStyleDefault-block\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Interactive Math Festival</span></p><ul class=\"carina-rte-public-DraftStyleDefault-ul\"><li>Large-scale hands-on math festival environment featuring multiple table-based activities designed to spark curiosity, collaboration, and joyful problem-solving for K–8 audiences.</li></ul><p class=\"carina-rte-public-DraftStyleDefault-block\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Are We There Yet? An Exploration of Distance</span></p><ul class=\"carina-rte-public-DraftStyleDefault-ul\"><li>Immersive multi-model math exploration combining physical builds, interactive puzzles, and VR to demonstrate different concepts of distance and geometry across mathematical systems.</li></ul><p class=\"carina-rte-public-DraftStyleDefault-block\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Math Card Game Exhibit</span></p><ul class=\"carina-rte-public-DraftStyleDefault-ul\"><li>Interactive math card game experience connecting middle school math concepts to real-world scenarios through collaborative, play-based problem solving.</li></ul><p class=\"carina-rte-public-DraftStyleDefault-block\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Sierpinski Simplices</span></p><ul class=\"carina-rte-public-DraftStyleDefault-ul\"><li>Collaborative fractal-building activity where participants construct a large Sierpinski tetrahedron through hands-on assembly, illustrating patterns, scaling, and mathematical structure.</li></ul></div></div>","id":"6fc13d53-6c76-4415-8dd6-32d6ba57f750","capacityId":"6fc13d53-6c76-4415-8dd6-32d6ba57f750","name":"Math Festival Day 1","status":2,"type":"Session","defaultFeeId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","fees":{},"closedReasonType":"NotClosed","isOpenForRegistration":false,"presentationType":"","categoryId":"54e36a9b-0bc7-4c6b-b196-76544c87e154","waitlistCapacityId":"6fc13d53-6c76-4415-8dd6-32d6ba57f750_waitlist","dataTagCode":"","startTime":"2026-07-24T18:00:00.000Z","endTime":"2026-07-24T22:00:00.000Z","locationId":"ca98ab39-5039-43e6-934e-5e7aa254dd53","locationName":"Hall E - Expo","locationCode":"Hall E - Expo","isIncludedSession":false,"isWaitlist