rities, and discuss some of its interactions with the (global) K-stability of Fano varieties and the Minimal Model Program.","plainTextDescription":"I will survey a local K-stability theory for Kawamata log terminal singularities, and discuss some of its interactions with the (global) K-stability of Fano varieties and the Minimal Model Program.","registrantInformation":"","displayPriority":0,"showOnAgenda":true,"isOpenForAttendeeHub":true,"featuredSession":false,"speakerIds":{"dad6abef-978d-40d0-bbaf-fc87690c2409":{"speakerId":"dad6abef-978d-40d0-bbaf-fc87690c2409","speakerCategoryId":"45ab9016-e39c-4327-8bdb-50c0e5f04916","sessionId":"fc0ea159-fa62-4785-bb7b-34e96f7dfb27","sessionSpeakerOrder":1}},"documents":{},"createdDate":"2025-04-11T14:49:56.810Z","restrictSessionVisibility":true},"a5b63f95-f231-41e5-b322-d94b410da1eb":{"code":"SCSNEHASISKUNDUSESSION","description":"The mean velocity distribution over the whole flow depth in smooth open channel turbulent flow usually consists of three parts: (i) the logarithmic law in the overlap layer; (ii) the wake law in the outer region; and (iii) the boundary correction. This work presents a simple law, referred to as the generalized law of the wake, which combines all three hypotheses into a single equation. This law, unlike the log-wake law, does not explicitly contain the wake function and the boundary corrections, but shows this in its inherent nature. The equation is derived from a general functional equation with the hypothesis of a wake factor as the linear span of the velocity function at two points. The general functional equation reverts to the functional equation previously proposed by Guo(2023) for the overlap layer as a special case. The general solution of the functional equation is also discussed as the general solution of a delayed-differential equation. The model is validated over a widespread range of experimental and river field data, and satisfactory results are obtained. This law expresses the measured data well over the entire flow domain.ReferencesGuo, J. (2023). The log-law of the wall in the overlap from a functional equation, Journal of Engineering Mechanics 149(2): 06022005-1– 06022005-3.","id":"a5b63f95-f231-41e5-b322-d94b410da1eb","capacityId":"a5b63f95-f231-41e5-b322-d94b410da1eb","name":"Generalized Law of the Wake with Dip Phenomenon for Smooth Open-Channel Turbulent Flows: A Functional Equation Approach","status":2,"type":"Session","defaultFeeId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","fees":{},"closedReasonType":"NotClosed","isOpenForRegistration":false,"presentationType":"","categoryId":"dd348cad-9fa9-4bfb-8f6b-0d76eda0f5fe","capacity":523,"waitlistCapacityId":"a5b63f95-f231-41e5-b322-d94b410da1eb_waitlist","dataTagCode":"","startTime":"2026-07-28T17:10:00.000Z","endTime":"2026-07-28T17:30:00.000Z","locationId":"832094e7-0e57-4e55-8e2e-d69b459e2551","locationName":"116-A","locationCode":"116-A","isIncludedSession":false,"isWaitlistEnabled":false,"registeredCount":1,"associatedWithAdmissionItems":[],"availableToAdmissionItems":[],"associatedRegistrationTypes":[],"sessionCustomFieldValues":{"1ff8930b-09e9-45ce-993d-1226c743588b":{"id":"1ff8930b-09e9-45ce-993d-1226c743588b","sessionId":"a5b63f95-f231-41e5-b322-d94b410da1eb","displayValue":"SNEHASIS KUNDU","answers":["SNEHASIS KUNDU"]},"ed161947-576f-4a6a-a4e1-5d22ce5a1203":{"id":"ed161947-576f-4a6a-a4e1-5d22ce5a1203","sessionId":"a5b63f95-f231-41e5-b322-d94b410da1eb","displayValue":"11 - Mathematical Physics","answers":["11 - Mathematical Physics"]}},"registrantInformation":"","displayPriority":0,"showOnAgenda":true,"isOpenForAttendeeHub":true,"featuredSession":false,"speakerIds":{"d08d16fc-4815-4cca-8e90-d877cfe5ad44":{"speakerId":"d08d16fc-4815-4cca-8e90-d877cfe5ad44","speakerCategoryId":"ab3cd2dc-d1f9-4200-a5a7-26b170cec2fb","sessionId":"a5b63f95-f231-41e5-b322-d94b410da1eb","sessionSpeakerOrder":0}},"documents":{},"createdDate":"2026-05-16T11:34:17.600Z","restrictSessionVisibility":true},"bf667a16