ations","answers":["10 - Partial Differential Equations"]}},"richTextDescription":"{\"format\":\"draftjs-nucleus\",\"version\":1,\"content\":{\"blocks\":[{\"key\":\"20tnr\",\"text\":\"Ideal fluid flows are dynamical rearrangements of space that minimize kinetic energy. Such flows, which solve the Euler equations, exhibit a wide range of interesting phenomena. We will give an overview of many of these phenomena, which have been rigorously established by many authors in recent years, and then focus mainly on questions related to steady solutions and finite-time singularities.\",\"type\":\"unstyled\",\"depth\":0,\"inlineStyleRanges\":[],\"entityRanges\":[],\"data\":{}}],\"entityMap\":{}}}","plainTextDescription":"Ideal fluid flows are dynamical rearrangements of space that minimize kinetic energy. Such flows, which solve the Euler equations, exhibit a wide range of interesting phenomena. We will give an overview of many of these phenomena, which have been rigorously established by many authors in recent years, and then focus mainly on questions related to steady solutions and finite-time singularities.","registrantInformation":"","displayPriority":0,"showOnAgenda":true,"isOpenForAttendeeHub":true,"featuredSession":false,"speakerIds":{"cd8071e3-b618-43e1-aec7-7ed8f2d7b7cd":{"speakerId":"cd8071e3-b618-43e1-aec7-7ed8f2d7b7cd","speakerCategoryId":"45ab9016-e39c-4327-8bdb-50c0e5f04916","sessionId":"22179016-50e4-4217-9c1a-00b1c78ac74f","sessionSpeakerOrder":1}},"documents":{},"createdDate":"2025-04-11T14:49:56.810Z","restrictSessionVisibility":true},"89f71480-4dde-4329-b177-74b8e34019aa":{"code":"SCThiHaDuongPHANSESSION","description":"<div class=\"ag87-crtemvc-hsbk\">Many complex systems can be modeled by very large graphs. Such graphs exhibit robustness, randomness, dynamic behavior, and distinctive structural features, while at the same time sharing several fundamental properties. A central issue in the study of complex systems is the partitioning of a population into communities, where each community exhibits common behavior and shared interests. Numerous research efforts have proposed and developed a variety of methodological approaches to address this problem.In this presentation, we will discuss models for large graphs and present algorithms for community detection, both with and without overlapping communities, based on random walk theory.</div>","id":"89f71480-4dde-4329-b177-74b8e34019aa","capacityId":"89f71480-4dde-4329-b177-74b8e34019aa","name":"XXX CANCELLED Complex Systems: Algorithms for Community Detection (Partitioning and Overlapping)","status":7,"type":"Session","defaultFeeId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","fees":{},"closedReasonType":"NotClosed","isOpenForRegistration":false,"presentationType":"","categoryId":"dd348cad-9fa9-4bfb-8f6b-0d76eda0f5fe","waitlistCapacityId":"89f71480-4dde-4329-b177-74b8e34019aa_waitlist","dataTagCode":"XXX CANCELLED Complex Sys","startTime":"2026-07-24T16:10:00.000Z","endTime":"2026-07-24T16:30:00.000Z","locationId":"832094e7-0e57-4e55-8e2e-d69b459e2551","locationName":"116-A","locationCode":"116-A","isIncludedSession":false,"isWaitlistEnabled":false,"registeredCount":0,"associatedWithAdmissionItems":[],"availableToAdmissionItems":[],"associatedRegistrationTypes":[],"sessionCustomFieldValues":{"ed161947-576f-4a6a-a4e1-5d22ce5a1203":{"id":"ed161947-576f-4a6a-a4e1-5d22ce5a1203","sessionId":"89f71480-4dde-4329-b177-74b8e34019aa","displayValue":"14 - Mathematics of Computer Science","answers":["14 - Mathematics of Computer Science"]}},"richTextDescription":"Many complex systems can be modeled by very large graphs. Such graphs exhibit robustness, randomness, dynamic behavior, and distinctive structural features, while at the same time sharing several fundamental properties. A central issue in the study of complex systems is the partitioning of a population into communities, where each community exhibits common behavior and shared interests. Numerous research efforts have proposed and developed a variety of methodological approaches to address this problem.In this presentation, we will discuss models for large graphs and present algorithms for community detection, both with and without overlapping communities, based on random walk theory.","plainTextDescription":"Many complex systems can be modeled by very large graphs. Such graphs exhibit robustness, randomness, dynamic behavior, and distinctive structural features, while at the same time sharing several fundamental properties. A central issue in the study of complex systems is the partitioning of a population into communities, where each community exhibits common behavior and shared interests. Numerous research efforts have proposed and developed a variety of methodological approaches to address this problem.In this presentation, we will discuss models for large graphs and present algorithms for community detection, both with and without overlapping communities, based on random walk theory.","registrantInformation":"","displayPriority":0,"showOnAgenda":false,"isOpenForAttendeeHub":false,"featuredSession":false,"speakerIds":{},"documents":{},"createdDate":"2026-05-16T11:49:56.663Z","restrictSessionVisibility":true},"0dee4454-e75f-432d-a72e-29de5d3ec2a1":{"code":"ICMFILM4","description":"<div class=\"ag87-crtemvc-hsbk\"><div class=\"css-vsf5of\"><p class=\"carina-rte-public-DraftStyleDefault-block\">Film Directed by George Csicsery<br><br><span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\">Journeys of Black Mathematicians: Forging Resilience is the first of a two-part documentary series produced by George Csicsery and Zala Films and developed in collaboration with </span>Tatitana<span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\"> Toro. <br><br>Simons Laufer Mathematical Sciences Institute and Johnny Houston, NAM that traces the evolution of a culture of Black scholars, scientists and educators. The film follows the stories of prominent pioneers, the challenges they faced and their triumphs as they are reflected in the success and contributions of today's productive Black mathematicians who followed them.<br><br>Panelists</span></p><ul class=\"carina-rte-public-DraftStyleDefault-ul\"><li style=\"text-align:left;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\">Dennis Davenport, Howard University </span></li><li style=\"text-align:left;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\">William Massey, Princeton University </span></li><li style=\"text-align:left;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\">Talithia Williams, Harvey Mudd College </span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\">Moderators: Johnny Houston and Aris Winger </span></li></ul></div></div>","id":"0dee4454-e75f-432d-a72e-29de5d3ec2a1","capacityId":"0dee4454-e75f-432d-a72e-29de5d3ec2a1","name":"Journeys of Black Mathematicians: Forging Resilience","status":2,"type":"Session","defaultFeeId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","fees":{},"closedReasonType":"NotClosed","isOpenForRegistration":false,"presentationType":"","categoryId":"749da546-7c7d-4d1d-9f6b-e44e7cf5dd74","capacity":130,"waitlistCapacityId":"0dee4454-e75f-432d-a72e-29de5d3ec2a1_waitlist","dataTagCode":"Journeys of Black Mathema","startTime":"2026-07-24T18:00:00.000Z","endTime":"2026-07-24T19:45:00.000Z","locationId":"8cc0c467-fc90-428c-9a6e-2940f2b4dead","locationName":"Benjamin Franklin Stage","locationCode":"Benjamin Franklin Stage","isIncludedSession":false,"isWaitlistEnabled":false,"registeredCount":60,"associatedWithAdmissionItems":[],"availableToAdmissionItems":[],"associatedRegistrationTypes":["5cb4f53d-aabf-4bc3-b876-8db33cba9ba5"],"sessionCustomFieldValues":{"c82e91fc-da7a-4a71-a7d5-32011a7a9b41":{"id":"c82e91fc-da7a-4a71-a7d5-32011a7a9b41","sessionId":"0dee4454-e75f-432d-a72e-29de5d3ec2a1","displayValue":"","answers":[]},"ed161947-576f-4a6a-a4e1-5d22ce5a1203":{"id":"ed161947-576f-4a6a-a4e1-5d22ce5a1203","sessionId":"0dee4454-e75f-432d-a72e-29de5d3ec2a1","displayValue":"","answers":[]}},"richTextDescription":"{\"format\":\"draftjs-nucleus\",\"version\":1,\"content\":{\"blocks\":[{\"key\":\"en7bd\",\"text\":\"Film Directed by George Csicsery\\n\\nJourneys of Black Mathematicians: Forging Resilience is the first of a two-part documentary series produced by George Csicsery and Zala Films and developed in collaboration with Tatitana Toro. \\n\\nSimons Laufer Mathematical Sciences Institute and Johnny Houston, NAM that traces the evolution of a culture of Black scholars, scientists and educators. The film follows the stories of prominent pioneers, the challenges they faced and their triumphs as they are reflected in the success and contributions of today's productive Black mathematicians who followed them.\\n\\nPanelists\",\"type\":\"unstyled\",\"depth\":0,\"inlineStyleRanges\":[{\"offset\":34,\"length\":178,\"style\":\"color-rgb(0,0,0)\"},{\"offset\":220,\"length\":387,\"style\":\"color-rgb(0,0,0)\"}],\"entityRanges\":[],\"data\":{}},{\"key\":\"7l74v\",\"text\":\"Dennis Davenport, Howard University \",\"type\":\"unordered-list-item\",\"depth\":0,\"inlineStyleRanges\":[{\"offset\":0,\"length\":36,\"style\":\"color-rgb(0,0,0)\"}],\"entityRanges\":[],\"data\":{\"text-align\":\"left\"}},{\"key\":\"19ukk\",\"text\":\"William Massey, Princeton University \",\"type\":\"unordered-list-item\",\"depth\":0,\"inlineStyleRanges\":[{\"offset\":0,\"length\":37,\"style\":\"color-rgb(0,0,0)\"}],\"entityRanges\":[],\"data\":{\"text-align\":\"left\"}},{\"key\":\"2ldqe\",\"text\":\"Talithia Williams, Harvey Mudd College \",\"type\":\"unordered-list-item\",\"depth\":0,\"inlineStyleRanges\":[{\"offset\":0,\"length\":39,\"style\":\"color-rgb(0,0,0)\"}],\"entityRanges\":[],\"data\":{\"text-align\":\"left\"}},{\"key\":\"abofh\",\"text\":\"Moderators: Johnny Houston and Aris Winger \",\"type\":\"unordered-list-item\",\"depth\":0,\"inlineStyleRanges\":[{\"offset\":0,\"length\":43,\"style\":\"color-rgb(0,0,0)\"}],\"entityRanges\":[],\"data\":{}}],\"entityMap\":{}}}","plainTextDescription":"Film Directed by George Csicsery\r\n\r\nJourneys of Black Mathematicians: Forging Resilience is the first of a two-part documentary series produced by George Csicsery and Zala Films and developed in collaboration with Tatitana Toro. \r\n\r\nSimons Laufer Mathematical Sciences Institute and Johnny Houston, NAM that traces the evolution of a culture of Black scholars, scientists and educators. The film follows the stories of prominent pioneers, the challenges they faced and their triumphs as they are reflected in the success and contributions of today's productive Black mathematicians who followed them.\r\n\r\nPanelists\r\nDennis Davenport, Howard University \r\nWilliam Massey, Princeton University \r\nTalithia Williams, Harvey Mudd College \r\nModerators: Johnny Houston and Aris Winger","registrantInformation":"All Full Attendees","displayPriority":0,"showOnAgenda":true,"isOpenForAttendeeHub":true,"featuredSession":false,"speakerIds":{},"documents":{},"createdDate":"2026-04-12T12:27:59.827Z","restrictSessionVisibility":true},"1502de7a-bc13-423b-99f5-fbc24527a6e8":{"code":"SCSYAMKUNCHAMSESSION","description":"On structural aspects of essential ideals in matrix nearrings and group nearringsSyam Prasad Kuncham#1, Rajani Salvankar2, Tapatee Sahoo3, Babushri Srinivas Kedukodi4 and Harikrishnan Panackal5 1,2,4,5Department of Mathematics, Manipal Institute of Technology,                                             Manipal Academy of Higher Education, Manipal – 576 104, India. 3Department of Mathematics, Manipal Institute of Technology Bengaluru Campus.Manipal Academy of Higher Education, Bengaluru-560064, India #Presenting Author: Email: syamprasad.k@manipal.eduAbstract Essential submodules play a vital role in the study of finite Goldie dimension in modules over associative rings. In this work, we extend these ideas to modules over nearrings. Nearrings are natural generalizations of associative rings in which addition need not be commutative and only one distributive law holds. We introduce the concept of essential ideals in matrix nearrings and establish several properties that highlight the interplay between nearrings and their corresponding matrix nearrings. Furthermore, we the study of essential ideals to group nearrings and explore their structural aspects. Finally, we prove the properties of graphs associated with these ideals and illustrate the results through suitable examples.AMS Classification: 16Y30Keywords: Matrix Nearring, Module over a Nearring, Essential ideal, Complement ideal # Presenting Author","id":"1502de7a-bc13-423b-99f5-fbc24527a6e8","capacityId":"1502de7a-bc13-423b-99f5-fbc24527a6e8","name":"On Structural Aspects of Essential Ideals in Matrix Nearrings and Group Nearrings","status":2,"type":"Session","defaultFeeId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","fees":{},"closedReasonType":"NotClosed","isOpenForRegistration":false,"presentationType":"","categoryId":"dd348cad-9fa9-4bfb-8f6b-0d76eda0f5fe","capacity":346,"waitlistCapacityId":"1502de7a-bc13-423b-99f5-fbc24527a6e8_waitlist","dataTagCode":"","startTime":"2026-07-25T16:50:00.000Z","endTime":"2026-07-25T17:10:00.000Z","locationId":"bc81cad2-8b75-45cb-9355-a764c88805b2","locationName":"120-AB","locationCode":"120-AB","isIncludedSession":false,"isWaitlistEnabled":false,"registeredCount":10,"associatedWithAdmissionItems":[],"availableToAdmissionItems":[],"associatedRegistrationTypes":[],"sessionCustomFieldValues":{"1ff8930b-09e9-45ce-993d-1226c743588b":{"id":"1ff8930b-09e9-45ce-993d-1226c743588b","sessionId":"1502de7a-bc13-423b-99f5-fbc24527a6e8","displayValue":"SYAM PRASAD KUNCHAM","answers":["SYAM PRASAD KUNCHAM"]},"ed161947-576f-4a6a-a4e1-5d22ce5a1203":{"id":"ed161947-576f-4a6a-a4e1-5d22ce5a1203","sessionId":"1502de7a-bc13-423b-99f5-fbc24527a6e8","displayValue":"2 - Algebra","answers":["2 - Algebra"]}},"registrantInformation":"","displayPriority":0,"showOnAgenda":true,"isOpenForAttendeeHub":true,"featuredSession":false,"speakerIds":{"ca4c443e-d62e-4b1c-ac0c-9625bc808a74":{"speakerId":"ca4c443e-d62e-4b1c-ac0c-9625bc808a74","speakerCatego