e to the constant heat and mass fluxes. It is shown thatthe constant heat, mass fluxes, and the radial surface tension cause the divergent motion at the interface and the Marangoni convectionbeneath the interface. Then, the linear stability of the steady thermo- and soluto-capillary convection in response to the azimuthal disturbanceis analyzed. At a given Peclet (or Schmidt), Marangoni (or Prandtl), and elasticity numbers, the steady basic flow loses its stability whenReynolds number is beyond the critical value. The critical patterns of the velocity fields and the isothermal, iso-concentration lines in the three-dimensional flow system in response to the disturbance harmonic wave number are dominated by both the radial and azimuthal surface tensions. This research is supported by the National Science Foundation through the Grants Nos. 11172310, 11472284 and 12272384.","id":"2f743de2-ba3a-485e-b076-3f4f8ce9be67","capacityId":"2f743de2-ba3a-485e-b076-3f4f8ce9be67","name":"Marangoni Convection and Instability Near the Air-Liquid Interface","status":2,"type":"Session","defaultFeeId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","fees":{},"closedReasonType":"NotClosed","isOpenForRegistration":false,"presentationType":"","categoryId":"dd348cad-9fa9-4bfb-8f6b-0d76eda0f5fe","capacity":706,"waitlistCapacityId":"2f743de2-ba3a-485e-b076-3f4f8ce9be67_waitlist","dataTagCode":"","startTime":"2026-07-27T15:50:00.000Z","endTime":"2026-07-27T16:10:00.000Z","locationId":"bc81cad2-8b75-45cb-9355-a764c88805b2","locationName":"120-AB","locationCode":"120-AB","isIncludedSession":false,"isWaitlistEnabled":false,"registeredCount":5,"associatedWithAdmissionItems":[],"availableToAdmissionItems":[],"associatedRegistrationTypes":[],"sessionCustomFieldValues":{"1ff8930b-09e9-45ce-993d-1226c743588b":{"id":"1ff8930b-09e9-45ce-993d-1226c743588b","sessionId":"2f743de2-ba3a-485e-b076-3f4f8ce9be67","displayValue":"Zuo-Bing Wu","answers":["Zuo-Bing Wu"]},"ed161947-576f-4a6a-a4e1-5d22ce5a1203":{"id":"ed1619