ems":[],"availableToAdmissionItems":[],"associatedRegistrationTypes":[],"sessionCustomFieldValues":{"1ff8930b-09e9-45ce-993d-1226c743588b":{"id":"1ff8930b-09e9-45ce-993d-1226c743588b","sessionId":"746a758a-8042-4dca-9f0a-f34f75aa0041","displayValue":"Susanne Brenner","answers":["Susanne Brenner"]},"ed161947-576f-4a6a-a4e1-5d22ce5a1203":{"id":"ed161947-576f-4a6a-a4e1-5d22ce5a1203","sessionId":"746a758a-8042-4dca-9f0a-f34f75aa0041","displayValue":"15 - Numerical Analysis and Scientific Computing","answers":["15 - Numerical Analysis and Scientific Computing"]}},"richTextDescription":"We present finite element methods that can capture smooth convex solutions of Monge-Ampere equations.  They are formulated as nonlinear least-squares problems on novel finite element spaces whose degrees of freedom can be used to enforce the local convexity of the finite element solutions.","plainTextDescription":"We present finite element methods that can capture smooth convex solutions of Monge-Ampere equations.  They are formulated as nonlinear least-squares problems on novel finite element spaces whose degrees of freedom can be used to enforce the local convexity of the finite element solutions.","registrantInformation":"","displayPriority":0,"showOnAgenda":true,"isOpenForAttendeeHub":true,"featuredSession":false,"speakerIds":{"80c3fad3-28e8-4004-ade1-5bc4115f77cf":{"speakerId":"80c3fad3-28e8-4004-ade1-5bc4115f77cf","speakerCategoryId":"45ab9016-e39c-4327-8bdb-50c0e5f04916","sessionId":"746a758a-8042-4dca-9f0a-f34f75aa0041","sessionSpeakerOrder":1}},"documents":{},"createdDate":"2025-04-11T14:49:56.810Z","restrictSessionVisibility":true},"0274a7b1-8f8c-47fe-a891-4961312cf0ac":{"code":"SCKpanzouSESSION","description":"This paper develops a general asymptotic representation (GAR) for a broad class of statistics based on two pivotal processes: the functional empirical process (fep) and the residual functional empirical process (lrfep) introduced by Lo and Sall (2010). By unifying their asymptotic behavior, we provide a versatile tool for deriving limit laws applicable to diverse statistical problems. When specialized to copula-based settings, these representations offer a rigorous foundation for comparing indices, whether temporally or across spatial domains, while accommodating complex dependence structures. The proposed framework bridges theoretical generality with practical utility, as demonstrated through explicit examples that highlight its implementation in real-world scenarios. Our results not only streamline asymptotic analysis for researchers working with empirical processes but also extend the methodological toolkit for index-based comparisons in econometrics, reliability analysis, and beyond. The paper concludes with applications underscoring the robustness and adaptability of the GAR approach, paving the way for future extensions in nonparametric and semiparametric inference.","id":"0274a7b1-8f8c-47fe-a891-4961312cf0ac","capacityId":"0274a7b1-8f8c-47fe-a891-4961312cf0ac","name":"XXX CANCELLED General Asymptotic Representations of Indexes Based on Functional Empirical Processes with Applications","status":2,"type":"Session","defaultFeeId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","fees":{},"closedReasonType":"NotClosed","isOpenForRegistration":false,"presentationType":"","categoryId":"dd348cad-9fa9-4bfb-8f6b-0d76eda0f5fe","waitlistCapacityId":"0274a7b1-8f8c-47fe-a891-4961312cf0ac_waitlist","dataTagCode":"","startTime":"2026-07-26T18:10:00.000Z","endTime":"2026-07-26T18:30:00.000Z","locationId":"832094e7-0e57-4e55-8e2e-d69b459e2551","locationName":"116-A","locationCode":"116-A","isIncludedSession":false,"isWaitlistEnabled":false,"registeredCount":0,"associatedWithAdmissionItems":[],"availableToAdmissionItems":[],"associatedRegistrationTypes":[],"sessionCustomFieldValues":{"1ff8930b-09e9-45ce-993d-1226c743588b":{"id":"1ff8930b-09e9-45ce-993d-1226c743588b","sessionId":"0274a7b1-8f8c-47fe-a891-4961312cf0ac","displayValue":"Tchilabalo Abozou Kpan