h\":0,\"inlineStyleRanges\":[],\"entityRanges\":[],\"data\":{}},{\"key\":\"382tl\",\"text\":\"Emily Braley\",\"type\":\"unordered-list-item\",\"depth\":0,\"inlineStyleRanges\":[],\"entityRanges\":[],\"data\":{}},{\"key\":\"404j4\",\"text\":\"Alex Kontorovich, Rutgers University \",\"type\":\"unordered-list-item\",\"depth\":0,\"inlineStyleRanges\":[],\"entityRanges\":[],\"data\":{}},{\"key\":\"b8j3t\",\"text\":\"Barbara Oakley, Oakland University\",\"type\":\"unordered-list-item\",\"depth\":0,\"inlineStyleRanges\":[],\"entityRanges\":[],\"data\":{}},{\"key\":\"52u23\",\"text\":\"\",\"type\":\"unstyled\",\"depth\":0,\"inlineStyleRanges\":[],\"entityRanges\":[],\"data\":{}}],\"entityMap\":{}}}","plainTextDescription":"Rapid advances in AI are providing challenges and opportunities in undergraduate mathematics education, for both teachers and learners.  We will attempt to give some perspective on a quickly-changing landscape:  disruptions in traditional assessment; new frontiers in personalized learning; experiments in pedagogy; and more.\nModerator: Ravi Vakil, Stanford University\nPanelists:  \nJarod Alper, University of Washington and Google Deepmind\nEmily Braley\nAlex Kontorovich, Rutgers University \nBarbara Oakley, Oakland University\n","registrantInformation":"All Full Attendees","displayPriority":0,"showOnAgenda":true,"isOpenForAttendeeHub":true,"featuredSession":false,"speakerIds":{"25fa5adb-6fd7-4dbc-86fe-9da405634c30":{"speakerId":"25fa5adb-6fd7-4dbc-86fe-9da405634c30","speakerCategoryId":"77c6f559-4c0c-4aed-92cc-5cf25bc7249b","sessionId":"5cdda3f4-2368-4d4c-9a7e-599698cfcc10","sessionSpeakerOrder":3},"0d24757e-fcb8-4b81-976b-3af9eefcadab":{"speakerId":"0d24757e-fcb8-4b81-976b-3af9eefcadab","speakerCategoryId":"77c6f559-4c0c-4aed-92cc-5cf25bc7249b","sessionId":"5cdda3f4-2368-4d4c-9a7e-599698cfcc10","sessionSpeakerOrder":5},"96c46545-4c2c-4214-a6dd-3c494f4bb860":{"speakerId":"96c46545-4c2c-4214-a6dd-3c494f4bb860","speakerCategoryId":"511871d9-2ffe-469e-af96-f3441b6be335","sessionId":"5cdda3f4-2368-4d4c-9a7e-599698cfcc10","sessionSpeakerOrder":4},"d801aa69-5220-492e-8837-6b784e34c2d7":{"speakerId":"d801aa69-5220-492e-8837-6b784e34c2d7","speakerCategoryId":"77c6f559-4c0c-4aed-92cc-5cf25bc7249b","sessionId":"5cdda3f4-2368-4d4c-9a7e-599698cfcc10","sessionSpeakerOrder":1},"650eb686-26b8-4ef4-baed-408c063c35f7":{"speakerId":"650eb686-26b8-4ef4-baed-408c063c35f7","speakerCategoryId":"cee6986f-c8ec-441f-94a0-81cee775f986","sessionId":"5cdda3f4-2368-4d4c-9a7e-599698cfcc10","sessionSpeakerOrder":2}},"documents":{},"createdDate":"2026-04-12T12:36:18.327Z","restrictSessionVisibility":true},"1e4e121c-0e82-49d8-956d-5a6174f1aecb":{"code":"SCMamataNandkeolyarSESSION","description":"<div class=\"ag87-crtemvc-hsbk\">This study presents a numerical analysis of the unsteady three-dimensional flow of a Casson fluid over a bi-directional stretching surface, considering the effects of Hall current, thermal radiation, homogeneous-heterogeneous reactions, viscous dissipation, and an external magnetic field. The flow is induced by the bi-directional stretching of the sheet in its plane. The presence of two different species in the flow region, participating in homogeneous and heterogeneous reactions, adds complexity to the problem. The fluid velocity, thermal, and mass transport are modelled using a set of nonlinear partial differential equations (PDEs) with appropriate boundary conditions. These PDEs are transformed into a set of nonlinear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) using similarity transformations. The transformed ODEs are then solved numerically using the bvp4c solver. The study presents a detailed analysis of the impact of various flow parameters on velocities, temperature, and concentration profiles through graphical representations. The results indicate that the thermal boundary layer thickness increases with higher Hall current, magnetic field strength, and thermal radiation. Conversely, mass transport decreases with higher homogeneous-heterogeneous reaction parameters. The study also calculates the physical quantities such as the coefficients of skin friction and heat and mass transfer.</div>","id":"1e4e121c-0e82-49d8-956d-5a6174f1aecb","capacityId":"1e4e121c-0e82-49d8-956d-5a6174f1aecb","name":"XXX CANCELLED Homogeneous-Heterogeneous Reactions, Hall Current, and Dissipative-Radiative Heat Transfer Effects on MHD Casson Fluid Flow Over a Bi-Directional Stretching Sheet","status":2,"type":"Session","defaultFeeId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","fees":{},"closedReasonType":"NotClosed","isOpenForRegistration":false,"presentationType":"","categoryId":"dd348cad-9fa9-4bfb-8f6b-0d76eda0f5fe","capacity":206,"waitlistCapacityId":"1e4e121c-0e82-49d8-956d-5a6174f1aecb_waitlist","dataTagCode":"XXX CANCELLED Homogeneous","startTime":"2026-07-27T16:50:00.000Z","endTime":"2026-07-27T17:10:00.000Z","locationId":"53df18b7-15a9-4d2e-8f2c-9445f7309783","locationName":"115-B","locationCode":"115-B","isIncludedSession":false,"isWaitlistEnabled":false,"registeredCount":0,"associatedWithAdmissionItems":[],"availableToAdmissionItems":[],"associatedRegistrationTypes":[],"sessionCustomFieldValues":{"1ff8930b-09e9-45ce-993d-1226c743588b":{"id":"1ff8930b-09e9-45ce-993d-1226c743588b","sessionId":"1e4e121c-0e82-49d8-956d-5a6174f1aecb","displayValue":"Mamata Nandkeolyar","answers":["Mamata Nandkeolyar"]},"ed161947-576f-4a6a-a4e1-5d22ce5a1203":{"id":"ed161947-576f-4a6a-a4e1-5d22ce5a1203","sessionId":"1e4e121c-0e82-49d8-956d-5a6174f1aecb","displayValue":"11 - Mathematical Physics","answers":["11 - Mathematical Physics"]}},"richTextDescription":"This study presents a numerical analysis of the unsteady three-dimensional flow of a Casson fluid over a bi-directional stretching surface, considering the effects of Hall current, thermal radiation, homogeneous-heterogeneous reactions, viscous dissipation, and an external magnetic field. The flow is induced by the bi-directional stretching of the sheet in its plane. The presence of two different species in the flow region, participating in homogeneous and heterogeneous reactions, adds complexity to the problem. The fluid velocity, thermal, and mass transport are modelled using a set of nonlinear partial differential equations (PDEs) with appropriate boundary conditions. These PDEs are transformed into a set of nonlinear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) using similarity transformations. The transformed ODEs are then solved numerically using the bvp4c solver. The study presents a detailed analysis of the impact of various flow parameters on velocities, temperature, and concentration profiles through graphical representations. The results indicate that the thermal boundary layer thickness increases with higher Hall current, magnetic field strength, and thermal radiation. Conversely, mass transport decreases with higher homogeneous-heterogeneous reaction parameters. The study also calculates the physical quantities such as the coefficients of skin friction and heat and mass transfer.","plainTextDescription":"This study presents a numerical analysis of the unsteady three-dimensional flow of a Casson fluid over a bi-directional stretching surface, considering the effects of Hall current, thermal radiation, homogeneous-heterogeneous reactions, viscous dissipation, and an external magnetic field. The flow is induced by the bi-directional stretching of the sheet in its plane. The presence of two different species in the flow region, participating in homogeneous and heterogeneous reactions, adds complexity to the problem. The fluid velocity, thermal, and mass transport are modelled using a set of nonlinear partial differential equations (PDEs) with appropriate boundary conditions. These PDEs are transformed into a set of nonlinear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) using similarity transformations. The transformed ODEs are then solved numerically using the bvp4c solver. The study presents a detailed analysis of the impact of various flow parameters on velocities, temperature, and concentration profiles through graphical representations. The results indicate that the thermal boundary layer thickness increases with higher Hall current, magnetic field strength, and thermal radiation. Conversely, mass transport decreases with higher homogeneous-heterogeneous reaction parameters. The study also calculates the physical quantities such as the coefficients of skin friction and heat and mass transfer.","registrantInformation":"","displayPriority":0,"showOnAgenda":false,"isOpenForAttendeeHub":false,"featuredSession":false,"speakerIds":{},"documents":{},"createdDate":"2026-05-16T11:46:06.753Z","restrictSessionVisibility":true},"16eb7a1f-4b39-495d-adf3-7e802176b2d7":{"code":"SCYoussefAzouziSESSION","description":"We present a general diagonalization process for nets, which extends the classical Cantor diagonal argument for sequences. While the countable version is constructive, the general form is not. Several applications are provided in functional analysis, topology, and the theory of vector and Banach lattices. We also show that our result allows for a simplification of the proofs of several known theorems.","id":"16eb7a1f-4b39-495d-adf3-7e802176b2d7","capacityId":"16eb7a1f-4b39-495d-adf3-7e802176b2d7","name":"Diagonal Process and Applications","status":2,"type":"Session","defaultFeeId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","fees":{},"closedReasonType":"NotClosed","isOpenForRegistration":false,"presentationType":"","categoryId":"dd348cad-9fa9-4bfb-8f6b-0d76eda0f5fe","waitlistCapacityId":"16eb7a1f-4b39-495d-adf3-7e802176b2d7_waitlist","dataTagCode":"","startTime":"2026-07-28T17:10:00.000Z","endTime":"2026-07-28T17:30:00.000Z","locationId":"bc81cad2-8b75-45cb-9355-a764c88805b2","locationName":"120-AB","locationCode":"120-AB","isIncludedSession":false,"isWaitlistEnabled":false,"registeredCount":5,"associatedWithAdmissionItems":[],"availableToAdmissionItems":[],"associatedRegistrationTypes":[],"session