                    "description": "<div class=\"ag87-crtemvc-hsbk\">The Mordell conjecture, proved by Faltings in 1983, asserts that there are only finitely many rational points on a curve of genus at least two over a number field. The uniform Mordell problem asks for suitable upper bounds on the number of rational points in the Mordell conjecture. In this talk, we will introduce various recent developments on this uniformity problem.</div>",
