                "df1420eb-395e-4335-93ad-e212d6fd43e0": {
                    "code": "SCBiniyamShimelisAliSESSION",
                    "description": "This study aims to create and examine fundamental properties of novel generalizations of the M-function using the framework of q-calculus. We construct several analytical properties of the suggested function, such as convergence requirements, recurrence relations, integral representations, q-derivative formulae, and the q-Laplace and q-Sumudu transformations. Additionally, picture formulations for the Caputo and Hilfer fractional q-derivatives are established. To demonstrate the applicability of the generated results, various specific scenarios and examples are studied. This paper adds to the continuing research on fractional q-integral operator relations for q-special functions, a fast emerging field of mathematical analysis. We use a q-analogue of the M-function to create a new fractional q-integral operator of Kober type. In addition, the generalized Kober-type fractional q-integral operator is used on the q-analogue of the H-function. As specific examples, findings for various well-known q-functions are given, including MacRobert's E-function, the q-analogues of the first and third classes of Bessel functions, the q-Struve functions, and basic hypergeometric functions. By investigating these linkages, this paper contributes to the theoretical underpinning of q-fractional calculus and offers up new options for future research and applications.",
