                    "code": "ÁgataTimónSession",
                    "description": "<div class=\"ag87-crtemvc-hsbk\">While mathematical research traditionally faces challenges achieving media visibility, this paper reflects on how strategic communication approaches might help overcome these barriers and foster public engagement. Drawing on practical experience from the Spanish Instituto de Ciencias Matemáticas (ICMAT)’s press office, we explore three potentially important elements: developing specialised communication infrastructure, strengthening communication pathways between the scientific community and news media, and employing narrative strategies tailored to mathematics’ distinct nature from other scientific disciplines. The paper identifies the specific communication challenges stemming from these characteristics, including high levels of abstraction, technical language, and complex public perceptions, and suggests strategies that have proven promising in our experience.</div>",
