                    "richTextDescription": "{\"format\":\"draftjs-nucleus\",\"version\":1,\"content\":{\"blocks\":[{\"key\":\"6alh0\",\"text\":\"Mural Arts Philadelphia has partnered with the Outreach Committee of the International Conress of Mathematicians (ICM) to create an indoor mural which is displayed at the 2026 ICM convening at the Pennsylvania Convention Center. This mural has engaged local students of the Mural Arts Foundations & Innovation program as well as local artist Oluwafemi as he directed them during the 2025 - 2026 school year to fabricate this piece.\",\"type\":\"unstyled\",\"depth\":0,\"inlineStyleRanges\":[],\"entityRanges\":[],\"data\":{}},{\"key\":\"7qbh9\",\"text\":\"The process has explored the intersections of art and mathematics through patterned tessellations and vibrant imagery that highlight the impact of mathematical research—career opportunities, groundbreaking discoveries, and the tools that shape innovation.\",\"type\":\"unstyled\",\"depth\":0,\"inlineStyleRanges\":[],\"entityRanges\":[],\"data\":{}},{\"key\":\"9eanu\",\"text\":\"Hear from the artist Oluwafemi during his talk on how the process unfolded as well as view a behind the scenes documentary capturing the makings of the mural.\",\"type\":\"unstyled\",\"depth\":0,\"inlineStyleRanges\":[],\"entityRanges\":[],\"data\":{}},{\"key\":\"dtl2n\",\"text\":\"This talk and view of the documentary will take place on the Benjamin Frankling Stage located within Hall E.\",\"type\":\"unstyled\",\"depth\":0,\"inlineStyleRanges\":[],\"entityRanges\":[],\"data\":{}}],\"entityMap\":{}}}",
                    "plainTextDescription": "Mural Arts Philadelphia has partnered with the Outreach Committee of the International Conress of Mathematicians (ICM) to create an indoor mural which is displayed at the 2026 ICM convening at the Pennsylvania Convention Center. This mural has engaged local students of the Mural Arts Foundations & Innovation program as well as local artist Oluwafemi as he directed them during the 2025 - 2026 school year to fabricate this piece.\r\nThe process has explored the intersections of art and mathematics through patterned tessellations and vibrant imagery that highlight the impact of mathematical research—career opportunities, groundbreaking discoveries, and the tools that shape innovation.\r\nHear from the artist Oluwafemi during his talk on how the process unfolded as well as view a behind the scenes documentary capturing the makings of the mural.\r\nThis talk and view of the documentary will take place on the Benjamin Frankling Stage located within Hall E.",
