                "c38f7376-71ea-4ea2-80ac-9c91c040129a": {
                    "code": "SCAasnaAasnaSESSION",
                    "description": "A streamline-diffusion finite element method (SDFEM) is applied to a coarse part of the spatial domain for a two-dimensional singularly perturbed degenerate parabolic problem defined on a unit square. Whereas the standard Galerkin finite element method (GFEM) is used on the dense part of the space domain to approximate the solution. Shishkin grids are constructed to partition the space domain into rectangular-shaped bilinear elements. The time-dependent derivative is discretized using the general $\\theta$- method, for $\\theta \\in [1/2,1]$, on a uniform temporal mesh. The solution of the considered problem contains two parabolic boundary layers on the left boundaries at $x=0$ and $y=0$. We derive the parameter uniform error estimates of $|||u_I - U_h|||_{SD}$ in the streamline-diffusion norm $||| \\cdot |||_{SD}$ for a suitable choice of stabilization parameter and show that the numerical solution $U_h$ is super-close to the bilinear interpolate $u_I$ of an exact solution $u$. These error estimates confirm that the total error $|||u-U_h|||_{SD}$ is not optimal. We introduce a discrete version of the SD-norm, and obtained an improved convergence result in the discrete norm $||| \\cdot |||_{SD,d}$. The proposed method yields parameter-uniform stability and convergence results both within and outside the layer region. Finally, all theoretical results are verified by taking some numerical experiments.",
                    "id": "c38f7376-71ea-4ea2-80ac-9c91c040129a",
                    "capacityId": "c38f7376-71ea-4ea2-80ac-9c91c040129a",
                    "name": "XXX CANCELLED A Robust Convergence Analysis of SDFEM for Two-Dimensional Singularly Perturbed Degenerate Parabolic Convection-Diffusion Problem",
