                    "description": "AbstractThis presentation focuses on generalizing classical sequence spaces to the bicomplex setting, where sequences consist of bicomplex numbers. We study their structural properties, including convergence and summability. We also explore how classical results extend or differ in this richer framework. Using the idempotent representation, we examine zero divisors and show how complex-valued results appear as special cases. This talk not only broadens the scope of existing sequence space theory but also suggests potential applications in bicomplex analysis and related mathematical areas.Keywords: Bicomplex numbers, Sequence spaces, Convergence and summability, Idempotent representation, Zero divisors.",
