                "18d8e8cf-8e03-4602-b522-ac52f5395da6": {
                    "code": "SCCristianVaySESSION",
                    "description": "<div class=\"ag87-crtemvc-hsbk\">We consider small quantum groups with root systems of Cartan, super and modular type, among others. These are constructed as Drinfeld doubles of finite-dimensional Nichols algebras of diagonal type. We discuss their connections with other algebras in the literature and highlight distinctive features of their representation theory. Based on the homonymous work by the author [Adv. Math. 475 (2025) 110347], we prove a linkage principle for them by adapting techniques from the work of Andersen, Jantzen and Soergel in the context of Lusztig’s small quantum groups. As a consequence, we characterize the blocks of the category of modules. We also introduce a notion of (a)typicality analogous to that appearing in the representation theory of Lie superalgebras. The typical simple modules turn out to be the simple and projective Verma modules. Moreover, we deduce a character formula for 1-atypical simple modules.</div>",
