                "0351a929-236a-4a81-97a7-c7cf6a1f5bd3": {
                    "code": "DzmitryDudkoSession",
                    "description": "<div class=\"ag87-crtemvc-hsbk\"><div class=css-vsf5of><p class=\"carina-rte-public-DraftStyleDefault-block\">The MLC Conjecture (the Mandelbrot set is Locally Connected) describes how quadratic polynomials depend topologically on a parameter. The Conjecture has many geometric and probabilistic counterparts; all of them are the subject of the Renormalization Theory, which analyzes first-return maps to small neighborhoods of special points. In this talk, we outline the current state of this theory, with particular emphasis on the (near-) zero-entropy or Molecule (satellite and neutral) regimes.</p></div></div>",
