                "838e567d-0eac-4e8c-96d4-5fc658d77732": {
                    "code": "SCSubuhiKhanSESSION",
                    "description": "<div class=\"ag87-crtemvc-hsbk\">In this study, the two-variable degenerate Hermite polynomials $\\mathcal{H}_m(z_1,z_2|\\tau)$ are contemplated using the formalism of group representation theory. These polynomials (2VDHP) are analyzed within the framework of an irreducible representation $\\uparrow'_{\\omega,\\mu}$ of the five-dimensional Lie algebra $\\mathcal{K}_{5}$. The general matrix elements of this representation are computed for the first time. Utilizing Lie algebraic techniques, specific results related to the structure and properties of the 2VDHP are established. Some examples are presented to derive implicit formulas for the polynomials associated with the 2VDHP $\\mathcal{H}_m(z_1,z_2|\\tau)$. Additionally, a Volterra-type integral equation satisfied by these polynomials is derived.  This work demonstrates the potential of extending the proposed methodology to other practical forms of degenerate Hermite polynomials encountered in mathematical physics, applied mathematics, and related scientific domains.</div>",
