                "e58191b1-af93-4470-92a2-bd811b8c98ef": {
                    "code": "SCZeynepKayarSESSION",
                    "description": "This paper focuses on establishing nabla and delta dynamic inequalities on time scales for the parameter range $0 < p < 1$. In contrast to the classical dynamic Hardy–Copson inequalities derived for $p > 1$, the inequalities presented herein do not preserve the direction observed in the classical cases. Instead, owing to the exponent lying within the interval $(0, 1)$, the direction of the resulting inequalities is reversed. Furthermore, the derived inequalities are not only novel but also provide a unified framework for continuous and discrete cases, addressing the parameter range $0 < p < 1$ which has previously been unexplored.",
