                    "description": "In this work, we develop an efficient numerical approach to deal with the time-fractional Benjamin-Bona-Mahony-Burger equations. The Benjamin-Bona-Mahony-Burger equation is a significant tool to describe the unidirectional propagation of long waves in specific nonlinear dispersive models. We utilize the Crank-Nicolson method in time with exponential B-splines in space. We establish convergence and stability of the proposed scheme. Due to the unavailability of the exact solution, the double mesh method is used for error estimates. The numerical simulations validate the theory, and a comparison with existing methods displays the efficacy of the proposed technique.",
