                "683f1baf-f396-4158-ac5f-06da2bafdc0d": {
                    "code": "SCNikitaAgarwalSESSION",
                    "description": "Let $S_g$ be the closed surface of genus $g$, $\\mathcal{L}$ be the infinite Jacob's ladder surface, and $\\text{Map}(S)$ denote the mapping class group of a surface $S$. Let $q_g:\\mathcal{L}\\rightarrow S_g$ be the regular infinite-sheeted cover with deck transformation group $\\mathbb{Z}$. In this talk, we show the existence of ``pseudo-Anosov-like\" maps on $\\mathcal{L}$ that arise as the lifts of Penner-type pseudo-Anosov maps on $S_g$ under the cover $q_g$. Furthermore, we establish that these lifts are topologically transitive, mixing, and support null recurrent dynamics. Moreover, we present concrete examples of infinite families of such maps on $\\mathcal{L}$.",
