                    "richTextDescription": "Many complex systems can be modeled by very large graphs. Such graphs exhibit robustness, randomness, dynamic behavior, and distinctive structural features, while at the same time sharing several fundamental properties. A central issue in the study of complex systems is the partitioning of a population into communities, where each community exhibits common behavior and shared interests. Numerous research efforts have proposed and developed a variety of methodological approaches to address this problem.In this presentation, we will discuss models for large graphs and present algorithms for community detection, both with and without overlapping communities, based on random walk theory.",
