                    "code": "SCOliviaNabawandaSESSION",
                    "description": "<div class=\"ag87-crtemvc-hsbk\">In this talk, we explore pattern avoidance of length $4$ in distinct flattened partitions, extending previous work on length-3 patterns. We classify all $24$ patterns into Wilf-equivalence classes and determine the corresponding avoidance sequences. Using structural decompositions, generating function techniques, and the kernel method, we solve functional equations and derive explicit algebraic formulas. The resulting sequences include classical families such as Catalan and Motzkin numbers, as well as new sequences arising from less symmetric classes.</div>",
