                "57abe5fb-fe1b-47f9-b277-514bca403e02": {
                    "code": "SCSaikatPatraSESSION",
                    "description": "<div class=\"ag87-crtemvc-hsbk\">In this talk, I will discuss completely positive trace-preserving maps, which are widely used in quantum information theory. These are mostly studied using the master equation perspective. A central part in this theory is to study whether a given system of dynamical maps $\\{\\Lambda_t: t \\ge 0\\}$ is CP-divisible or not CP-divisible. We study the problem when the underlying Hilbert space is of infinite dimensional. In special case, we describe condition of divisibility for Gaussian channel. For one parameter family of $n$-mode Gaussian channel and give explicit condition for its P-divisibility and CP-divisibility. We also note that our method of detecting P-divisibility and CP-divisibility for $n$-mode Gaussian channels is easier and more general than the method was given by  [\\href{PhysRevLett.118.050401}{Gerardo Adesso et.al PhysRevLett.118.050401}] which only deals with $1$-mode Gaussian channels with the same assumptions.</div>",
