                "fbb21cef-8d1a-4d6d-820d-9e6e2086771f": {
                    "code": "SCAlexCarlucciRezendeSESSION",
                    "description": "We investigate the behavior of the period function in a family of planar piecewise Hamiltonian systems. Special attention is given to its monotonicity properties and the occurrence of critical periods. A complete bifurcation diagram is derived, highlighting parameter regions where the period function is strictly increasing or decreasing, as well as regions where it admits at most one simple critical period. The analysis is based on decomposing the period function into contributions from the underlying planar Hamiltonian systems on each side of the discontinuity line, which are then carefully combined to capture the global dynamics.",
