                    "code": "SCArdelineMaryBuhphangSESSION",
                    "description": "In this talk we show that for any graph $E$ and for a commutative unital ring $R$, the nil ideals of the Leavitt path algebra $L_R(E)$ depend solely on the nil ideals of the ring $R$. We also obtain results on the Jacobson radical of $L_R(E)$ for a graph $E$ with no regular vertex. Additionally, we obtain that for a nil ideal $I$ of a Leavitt path algebra $L_{R}(E)$, the ideal $M_2(I)$ is also nil thus establishing that Leavitt path algebras over arbitrary graphs satisfy the K$\\ddot{o}$ethe's conjecture.",
                    "id": "e057a742-44af-4b57-a42e-106ff0e0d0be",
