                    "description": "<div class=\"ag87-crtemvc-hsbk\"><div class=css-vsf5of><p class=\"carina-rte-public-DraftStyleDefault-block\">The words figure and symbol are frequently employed to describe features of mathematical texts. However, what counts as a figure or a symbol within mathematics is unstable over time, place, individual, and research domain. This talk documents the value of this plasticity in the work of the geometer Charlotte Angas Scott and her students at the turn of the twentieth century.</p></div></div>",
