                    "code": "SCSarikaGoyalSESSION",
                    "description": "In this poster, I will discuss necessary and sufficient conditions on the perturbation $\\rho$ for the existence of positive least energy solutions of the critical singular semilinear elliptic equation  $ -\\Delta u = \\frac{|u|^{2^{*}(s)-2}}{|x|^s}u + \\rho(u) $  with Dirichlet boundary condition in a bounded smooth domain in $\\mathbb R^n$ containing the origin, where  $2^*(s)=\\frac{2(n-s)}{n-2}$ with  $0\\leq s<2$. Moreover we show that the almost necessary and sufficient condition obtained for the case $s=0$ in [1] differs conceptually when $0<s<2$.  \\\\[1] Adimurthi,  Mancini, G. and Sandeep, K. A sharp solvability condition in higher dimensions for some Brezis-Nirenberg type equation. Calc Var 14, 275–317 (2002). https://doi.org/10.1007/s005260100100",
