                    "code": "SCTitaKhalisSESSION",
                    "description": "Let $G$ be a graph of order $p$ without isolated vertices. A bijection $f: V(G) \\to  \\{1,2,3,\\dots,p\\}$ is called a local distance antimagic labeling, if $w_f(u)\\ne w_f(v)$ for every edge $uv$ of $G$, where $w_f(u)=\\sum_{x\\epsilon N(u)} {f(x)}$. The local distance antimagic chromatic number $\\chi_{lda}(G)$ is defined to be the minimum number of colors taken over all colorings of $G$ induced by local distance antimagic labelings of $G$.  In this paper, we present a sufficient condition for a graph $G$ to have $\\chi_{lda}(G) = |V(G)|$ and determine some family of graphs $G$ whose $\\chi_{lda}(G) = |V(G)|$.",
