                "f8e1fd47-906e-44b3-9fa7-a2b0f6e55701": {
                    "code": "SCRashiLuniaSESSION",
                    "description": "In 2008, Soundararajan introduced the resonance method and showed the existence of a normalized Hecke eigenform $f$ of weight $k$ and level one such that $L(s, f )$ takes large values at $s = 1/2$ for sufficiently large $k \\equiv 0 \\pmod{4}$. In this talk, we will discuss a recent work with Sanoli Gun, where we study how often $L(s, f )$ attains such large values at $s = 1/2$. We further investigate this question for $L$-functions attached to quadratic twists of $f$. Finally we give applications of our results to the theory of half-integer weight modular forms.",
