                    "description": "<div class=\"ag87-crtemvc-hsbk\">The present research work is the analysis of stress and temperature distribution in a functionally graded fractal thermo-triclinic solid half-space immersed in an infinite inviscid liquid. The governing equations of a functionally graded triclinic thermoelastic medium are formulated in context of generalized Fourier  heat law. The coupled wave equations obtained in terms of displacement, functionally gradation parameter and temperature are solved using wave solutions. The components of displacement, stresses and temperature field in the medium are obtained and presented graphically under the action of mechanical/thermal source along the free surface of the triclinic thermoelastic medium. The effect of functionally gradation (non-homogeneity) parameter and anisotropy is investigated and shown graphically.</div>",
