                "7f82442b-be0c-490f-ba2b-738c9759cc67": {
                    "code": "ShiriArtstein-AvidanSession",
                    "description": "<div class=\"ag87-crtemvc-hsbk\">We explore the field of convex geometric analysis through the prism of duality theory. We discuss the theoretical basis of, and the motivation for, studying order reversing involutions, mainly on classes of convex sets and functions. We discuss the different dualities which can appear and which share some basic structure, and their uniqueness. We give special emphasis on three main non-traditional examples, pertaining to geometric convex functions, pseudo-cones, and ball bodies. We use the Blaschke-Santal\\'o inequalty from convex geometry as a testing ground for these dualities.</div>",
                    "id": "7f82442b-be0c-490f-ba2b-738c9759cc67",
