                "85f1cefe-ff49-4d53-8d3a-03d05112d88b": {
                    "code": "SCVarshaChauhanSESSION",
                    "description": "Additive codes over finite fields naturally generalize linear codes and play a significant role in the construction of quantum error-correcting codes.  In this talk, for an integer $m \\geq 2$ and a prime power $q,$ we will discuss about the locality properties of $\\mathbb{F}_q$-additive MDS codes over $\\mathbb{F}_{q^{m}}$ whose dual codes are also MDS. Among the family of $\\mathbb{F}_q$-additive codes over $\\mathbb{F}_{q^{m}},$ which are not MDS, we will provide a method to construct optimal and almost optimal LRCs with new parameters. More specifically, we will provide a method to construct optimal and almost optimal $\\mathbb{F}_q$-additive  LRCs  over $\\mathbb{F}_{q^{m}}$ with locality $r$ that relies on the existence of certain special polynomials over $\\mathbb{F}_q,$ which we shall refer to as $(r,m)$-good polynomials over $\\mathbb{F}_q,$ (note that $(r,m)$-good polynomials over $\\mathbb{F}_q$ coincide with $r$-good polynomials over $\\mathbb{F}_{q}$ when $m=1$). We will also derive sufficient conditions under which   $\\mathbb{F}_q$-additive LRCs over $\\mathbb{F}_{q^{m}}$ constructed using the proposed method are optimal. We will further provide four general methods to construct $(r,m)$-good polynomials over $\\mathbb{F}_q,$ which give rise to several classes of optimal and almost optimal LRCs over $\\mathbb{F}_{q^{m}}$ with locality $r.$  To demonstrate these results, we will list several optimal  LRCs over $\\mathbb{F}_{q^{m}} $ with new parameters. Finally, we will consider the case $m=1$ and obtain some new  $r$-good polynomials over $\\mathbb{F}_q,$ which give rise to a construction of optimal linear LRCs over $\\mathbb{F}_q$ with locality $r.$  We will demonstrate this result by listing several optimal linear LRCs over smaller finite fields compared to the previously known LRCs with the same parameters.",
                    "id": "85f1cefe-ff49-4d53-8d3a-03d05112d88b",
                    "capacityId": "85f1cefe-ff49-4d53-8d3a-03d05112d88b",
