                "1f0447f8-c32a-4203-bc27-a56abdcd43c1": {
                    "code": "SCMINHAJULMINHAJULSESSION",
                    "description": "In this talk, we consider the Riemann problem and wave interactions for the one-dimensional generalized Chaplygin gas equations with a nonlinear time-dependent source term. We discuss the construction of the Riemann solution for this nonhomogeneous hyperbolic system and show that the solution contains a singularity under certain conditions in the initial data; that is, a $\\delta$-shock wave arises in the solution. Consequently, we derive the speed, position, and strength of the $\\delta$-shock using the $\\delta$-entropy condition. Finally, we discuss the wave interactions involving the $\\delta$-shock wave to establish the global solution by taking three piecewise constant perturbed initial data.",
                    "id": "1f0447f8-c32a-4203-bc27-a56abdcd43c1",
                    "capacityId": "1f0447f8-c32a-4203-bc27-a56abdcd43c1",
                    "name": "Riemann Problem and Delta Shock Interactions in Generalized Chaplygin Gas with Source Term",
