                    "code": "SCFNURakviSESSION",
                    "description": "In the 1970s, Serre proved that the adelic index of a non-CM elliptic curve over a number field is finite. More recently, Zywina conjectured the complete set of adelic indices for such curves over $\\mathbb{Q}$. In this talk, we discuss a recent joint work with Kate Finnerty, Tyler Genao and Jacob Mayle in which we prove that Zywina's conjecture is true for the family of non-CM elliptic curves over $\\mathbb{Q}$ that admit a nontrivial rational cyclic isogeny. This strengthens a result of Lemos that resolved Serre's uniformity question for the same family of curves.",
