                "a16b897a-aab4-44f9-9ccd-2ef0bc8af64c": {
                    "code": "CarlosLópez LeivaSession",
                    "description": "<div class=\"ag87-crtemvc-hsbk\">My goal in this session is to introduce the work done with bilingual (Spanish and English) students exploring, animating, and expressing mathematical concepts. The expressions and concepts that we have experienced in the bilingual classroom have helped us note that wonder as much as languaging are essential in the process of embodying mathematical concepts and feeling our connections to them and ourselves. Furthermore, in this process, I will conceptualize how the assemblages formed among students, objects, adults, and expressions—embedded in the physical and discursive animation of mathematical concepts—move through a translanguaging corriente or stream, which is nurtured through a mutual noticing and being with each other in the here and now. The sharing of our experiences facilitating and doing this work will be used as a platform to engage the participants in sharing their expressions on how this approach resonates with them and their contexts.</div>",
