                    "code": "SCÖmerYapmanSESSION",
                    "description": "This study presents a computational method of the first order for solving Volterra–Fredholm integro-differential equations with boundary layers. A numerical finite difference scheme is constructed on a uniform mesh. This is achieved by using the composite right-sided rectangle formula for the integral part, and interpolating quadrature rules and linear exponential basis functions for the differential part. It is demonstrated that the numerical scheme achieves first-order accuracy and uniformly converges with respect to the small ε-parameter. The efficacy of this approach is demonstrated by examining the performance of the numerical scheme in a single example.",
