                "d683387c-5a79-4f3e-b7e0-748394b842d1": {
                    "code": "SCRafiqulIslamSESSION",
                    "description": "We introduce new developments in sampling theory based on higher-order Langevin Monte Carlo and decentralized stochastic gradient Langevin methods. Building on recent advances in Langevin dynamics of arbitrary order, we establish non-asymptotic Wasserstein convergence guarantees that improve the dependence of mixing times on dimension and accuracy. In parallel, we extend the EXTRA framework from decentralized optimization to Langevin-based sampling, thereby removing network-induced bias in distributed Bayesian inference. Our results enhance two directions—higher-order dynamics and consensus-based sampling—offering rigorous iteration complexity bounds together with provable scalability in multi-agent networks.",
