                "c13db0fb-7ec1-4c1c-88e3-52692215ed6c": {
                    "code": "SCAprameyoPalSESSION",
                    "description": "The goal is to explain factorization phenomena for certain $p$-adic $L$-functions, guided by the Artin formalism. I will begin by recalling some background and previously known results in the setting of $\\mathrm{GL}_2$ and $\\mathrm{GL}_2 \\times \\mathrm{GL}_2$. I will then describe some of our recent work on factorization problems for triple products of Hida families and for twisted triple products of Hilbert modular forms over real quadratic fields. The proofs are largely based on comparisons between different Euler systems arising in these settings. Finally, I will give sketches of the proofs in selected cases, illustrating both analytic and algebraic factorization results, with an emphasis on the main ideas rather than technical details. These are joint works with K. B\\\"uy\\\"ukboduk,  D. Casazza, CdV Piquero and B. Das.",
