                    "code": "SCEmanuelGuarigliaSESSION",
                    "description": "In this short communication, we deal with new analytic results concerning fractional calculus of zeta functions. First, we study the zero-free regions of the $\\alpha$-order fractional derivative of the Riemann zeta function. In particular, we show some zero-free regions of $\\zeta^{(\\alpha)}(s)$. Furthermore, we prove existence of a zero-free region in the left half-plane depending on the complement of a circle of finite radius $r_{\\alpha}$ centered at the origin. In the second part, we prove and discuss the property of universality of $\\zeta^{(\\alpha)}(s)$. As a consequence, a wide class of analytic functions can be approximated by shifts of $\\zeta^{(\\alpha)}(s + i \\tau)$, $\\tau \\in \\mathbb{R}$.",
