                "5a14672c-d80b-463a-b253-e94286d8d19c": {
                    "code": "SCMengweiHuSESSION",
                    "description": "Kleinian singularities are quotients of $\\mathbb{C}^2$ by finite subgroups of  $\\mathrm{SL}_2(\\mathbb{C})$. They are in bijection with the ADE Dynkin diagrams via the McKay correspondence. The filtered Poisson deformations of Kleinian singularities are parametrized by $\\mathfrak{h}/W$, where $\\mathfrak{h}$ is the Cartan space and $W$ is the Weyl group. In this talk, I will introduce certain singular Lagrangian subvarieties in the deformations and resolutions of Kleinian singularities that are related to the geometric classification of certain Harish-Chandra modules over quantizations of nilpotent orbits. The irreducible components of these singular Lagrangian subvarieties are projective lines and affine curves. I will describe how they intersect with each other through the realization of deformations of Kleinian singularities as Nakajima quiver varieties.",
