                    "code": "JenniferBalakrishnanSession",
                    "description": "<div class=\"ag87-crtemvc-hsbk\">We survey explicit p-adic methods  for determining sets of rational points on curves of genus 2 or more, after the work of Chabauty.  This starts with the work of Coleman in 1985, which was then reframed by Kim's foundational work on Selmer varieties, and made explicit in certain cases by Balakrishnan, Besser, Dogra, Muller, Tuitman, and Vonk over the last decade. We highlight notable curves where these methods have succeeded and discuss related recent work.</div>",
