                    "code": "SCSurenaHozooriSESSION",
                    "description": "We will discuss some recent developments in the contact geometric theory of Anosov 3-flows, whose roots go back to the works of Mitsumatsu and Eliashberg-Thurston in the mid 1990s. In particular, we provide a contact geometric characterization of Anosov 3-flows based on interactions with Reeb dynamics, as well as investigate some properties of the resulting geometries. We will briefly highlight how these results allow one to re-approach some classical open questions in Anosov dynamics.",
