                    "description": "This research explores extensions to the successive lumping method for Markov chains and processes, originally constrained by the requirement of entrance states. Successive lumpability enables the stationary distribution of a Markov chain to be derived by computing the stationary probabilities of a sequence of reduced chains. While the entrance state condition ensures feasibility in this approach, its strictness limits applicability. Here, we investigate methods to relax or bypass this requirement, including the construction of artificial entrance states and leveraging structural properties of specific Markov processes.",
