                "61b62444-1371-45c7-a122-2a8480677f61": {
                    "code": "SCArmelANDAMIOVONOSESSION",
                    "description": "One of the types of problem that have attracted mathematicians attention in recent years is phase-field system models. In our talk, we focus on a generalisation of the Caginalp phase field system derived from the Maxwell-Cattaneo law on the one hand, and from the two-temperature theory of heat conduction on the other. We first show that the problem is well posed and obtain dissipativity properties of the associated solution operators. We then prove estimates $L^\\infty$-estimates relying on regularity estimates based on Moser's iterations. We finally analyze a spatial behaviour of the solution in a semi-infinite cylinder, when such solutions exist.",
