                "title": "PhD Student",
                "code": "PPYusenGuo",
                "biography": "I am a doctoral researcher in Applied Mathematics and Scientific Computing at the University of Leicester, with a background in mathematics from Imperial College London. My research focuses on robust finite element methods and adjoint-based PDE-constrained optimization for electromagnetic problems.Specifically, I develop algorithms to control magnetic fields through the design of metastructures. This requires solving nonlinear, time-dependent Maxwell's equations (H-formulation) subject to spatial and material constraints. My most recent work, published in Science Advances (2025), introduced a novel framework for designing magnetic cloaks for arbitrary, real-world geometries using adjoint-based optimization. This approach moves beyond the traditional analytical solution to the cloaking problem, employing advanced mathematical methods to enable the design of customizable magnetic shields for applications in fusion energy and medical technology.",
