                "biography": "An Ky (Kyan) Duy Nguyen is a second-year PhD student in Mathematics in the Department of Mathematical and Physical Sciences at La Trobe University. His research focuses on Lie theory, geometric analysis, and Riemannian and differential geometry, with particular emphasis on the geometry and topology of symmetric and homogeneous spaces. He works under the supervision of Associate Professor Yuri Nikolayevsky and Professor Vladimir Matveev.Kyan holds a Master of Science (Research) and a Bachelor of Science with First Class Honours in Mathematics from La Trobe University, achieving outstanding academic results. His research has led to multiple publications and preprints on Killing tensors, homogeneous geodesics, and Lie groups, including work published in the Journal of Lie Theory. He has presented his work at international conferences and workshops in geometry and mathematical physics and is the recipient of several competitive scholarships, fellowships, and research travel awards.",
